<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Dec consumer price index up 9.4 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>S.African Dec consumer price index up 9.4 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-items consumer price index rose 1.0 percent in December from November after rising 0.4 percent in November, the Central Statistical Service said.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise was 9.4 percent versus November's 9.2 percent and brought the average rate for the year to 7.4 pct compared with 8.7 percent in 1995, the lowest since 1972 when the average rate was 6.1 percent.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast a 1.0 percent month-on-month increase and a 9.6 percent year-on-year rise.  </p>
<p>Pct changes:</p>
<p>			 Year/year			     Month/month</p>
<p>			 Dec '96    Nov '96  Dec '95  -  latest  prev</p>
<p>All items	    9.4	   9.2     6.9	   1.0     0.4</p>
<p>Lower income gp    9.1	   9.3     7.0	   0.9     0.3</p>
<p>Middle income gp   9.8	   9.6     7.1	   1.0     0.4</p>
<p>Higher income gp   9.3	   9.0     6.8	   1.0     0.4</p>
<p>Food only	    9.9	  11.6     3.6	   1.1     0.0</p>
